From: silentsudin <25103587+silentsudin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 17:03:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] cpu: fix Intel RAPL CPU power readings

- Add a shared RaplCounter helper (src/rapl.h) that converts energy_uj to
  watts with floating point math, real timestamps and wraparound handling
  through max_energy_range_uj.
- Prefer the MSR based intel-rapl zone over intel-rapl-mmio for package-0.
- Subtract the "uncore" domain (the iGPU on Intel client parts) from
  package power, so the iGPU is not reported as CPU power as well.
- Keep retrying sensor discovery every 5 seconds instead of giving up after
  five attempts, so permissions granted after startup take effect.
- Warn (instead of a debug message) when energy_uj is not readable.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
